From: Djair Guilherme <djair.jr@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: 8250_dw: only try DMA when "dmas" is described

The driver hooked up DMA for every port with a FIFO; on boards whose DT
gives the UART no dmas the request can only fail, and each open logged
"failed to request DMA" before falling back to PIO.

diff --color -ruN a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c	2026-10-18 12:28:21.702527569 -0300
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_dw.c	2026-10-18 12:28:21.747968987 -0300
@@ -759,8 +759,12 @@
 	if (!data->skip_autocfg)
 		dw8250_setup_port(p);
 
-	/* If we have a valid fifosize, try hooking up DMA */
-	if (p->fifosize) {
+	/*
+	 * If we have a valid fifosize and the firmware describes DMA channels,
+	 * try hooking up DMA.  Without "dmas" the request can only fail, and
+	 * every open logged "failed to request DMA" before falling back to PIO.
+	 */
+	if (p->fifosize && device_property_present(p->dev, "dmas")) {
 		data->data.dma.rxconf.src_maxburst = p->fifosize / 4;
 		data->data.dma.txconf.dst_maxburst = p->fifosize / 4;
 		up->dma = &data->data.dma;
